Session logs and per-analysis captures — contents not tracked in git (see .gitignore)
=====================================================================================

This file only keeps the directory in a fresh clone; everything else here is a per-run
artifact written by the application, never committed. The application also creates the
directory itself if it is missing (src/Logger/Core.py).

What lands here
---------------
    logger/log_<date>_<HH-MM>.txt    one session log per application start (Logger/Core.py)
    logger/log_<Hardware>.csv        the run summary, one row per analysis, named after the
                                     loaded configuration's hardware id (log_unconfigured.csv
                                     before one is loaded); an older column set is archived
                                     beside it rather than overwritten
    logger/captures/                 each analysis's capture set — the frames, annotated
                                     image, label mask, _objects.json and _understanding.txt,
                                     bounded to the newest 50 sets (UI/Capture.py)

All of it can be deleted between sessions; nothing the application needs to start is kept here.
